+++ b/test/manual/olmicro/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,132 @@
+# Native Olmicro qualification
+
+Source baseline: SGLang `3145136dcd1238754e0ea2b2ffd546532119c71c`.
+The model implementation is `sglang.srt.models.mainline_ladder` and uses
+SGLang's packed GDN Triton kernels, managed convolution/recurrent state, and
+paged full attention through the native `fa3` backend. It never invokes the Transformers model forward.
+
+Initial scope: BF16, TP1/PP1, FP32 recurrent state, eager execution, no prefix
+cache, no quantization or speculative decoding. All five release sizes use
+the same architecture implementation. Enabling other modes needs qualification.
+The standard GDN beta range is extended to `[0,2]` for the release checkpoints;
+other models retain the default scale of one.
+
+Plain RMSNorm rounds the normalized activation to BF16 before the learned
+weight multiply, matching [vLLM's CUDA implementation](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/v0.19.1/csrc/layernorm_kernels.cu#L74).
+SGLang uses its batched GPU implementation where the cast-before-multiply JIT
+kernel does not support a width, including 640. Doubled-beta sigmoid/scale stay
+FP32 in both prefill and decode; the prefill tensor's FP32 dtype alone does not
+guarantee that intermediates avoided BF16 rounding. QKV and gate/up matrices,
+like the depthwise filters, are packed at weight load while preserving all
+release parameter names and supporting partial updates. The Olmicro-only chunk
+solve rounds beta*K before its Gram product and uses IEEE block merges. The
+fused SwiGLU kernel preserves the BF16 SiLU intermediate used by the qualified
+vLLM reference. Other SGLang models retain their existing GDN arithmetic.
+
+## Reproduce
+
+Set `SGLANG_USE_SGL_FA3_KERNEL=1` to use the image's pinned native kernels.
+Use a pinned SGLang environment with this checkout's `python/` first on
+`PYTHONPATH`. Unset `SGLANG_EXTERNAL_MODEL_PACKAGE` and
+`MILES_HYBRID_REFERENCE_BACKBONE`; the probe does this before importing SGLang.
+Use the qualified Core/vLLM image in a separate process for the second probe.
+Never load both engines onto the GPU simultaneously.
+
+```bash
+python -m pytest -q test/manual/olmicro/test_config.py \
+  test/manual/olmicro/test_beta_scale.py test/manual/olmicro/test_weight_loading.py \
+  test/manual/olmicro/test_probe_backend.py test/manual/olmicro/test_distribution.py \
+  test/manual/olmicro/test_norm.py test/manual/olmicro/test_chunk_precision.py \
+  test/manual/olmicro/test_activation.py
+python test/manual/olmicro/probe_backend.py --backend sglang --attention-backend fa3 \
+  --model "$CHECKPOINT" --output sglang.json
+python test/manual/olmicro/probe_backend.py --backend vllm \
+  --model "$CHECKPOINT" --output vllm.json
+python test/manual/olmicro/probe_backend.py \
+  --compare sglang.json vllm.json --output parity.json
+```
+
+The default probe uses prompt lengths 1, 3, 31, 127, 511, 2047 and 3071;
+32 greedy decode tokens; 16 concurrent slots; 19 queued requests; reordered
+slot reuse; and SGLang same-checkpoint reload. It checks selected-token
+log probabilities on identical teacher-forced inputs (maximum absolute error
+0.08). Greedy branch differences are reported separately. This is not a
+full-vocabulary KL or RL weight-publication qualification.
+
+The separate distribution probe scores the full vocabulary at every position
+of the fixed continuation, plus the repeated-question boundary (50 prefixes
+with the default lengths). It uses one request at a time to bound transport
+memory, validates normalization and identity, and reports both KL directions
+and total variation. Its maximum bidirectional KL gate is 1e-3. It complements
+the selected-token and exact greedy checks; their failures remain visible.
+
+```bash
+python test/manual/olmicro/probe_distribution.py --backend sglang --attention-backend fa3 \
+  --model "$CHECKPOINT" --output distribution-sglang.pt
+python test/manual/olmicro/probe_distribution.py --backend vllm \
+  --model "$CHECKPOINT" --output distribution-vllm.pt
+python test/manual/olmicro/probe_distribution.py \
+  --compare distribution-sglang.pt distribution-vllm.pt --output distribution-parity.json
+```
+
+Use the same read-only checkpoint and GPU class for both backends. The general
+midtrain checkpoints are under
+`/weka/oe-training-default/yashasbls/hybridish-local/hf/v1/SIZE/midtrain/STEP`:
+
+| Size | Step directory |
+|---|---|
+| 275m | step0038147 |
+| 450m | step0038147 |
+| 810m | step0023842 |
+| 1.4b | step0011921 |
+| 2.7b | step0011921 |
+
+## Interactive qualification, 2026-10-30
+
+Beaker session: https://beaker.org/job/01M675BCQ9F5G11AP6DEAAMAAW (one Neptune
+L40S, two-hour limit). SGLang image `01M607Z48PYPNN0KHVZ5PGYJEG`, source overlay
+under `/opt/olmicro-native`. CUDA 13 requires this session-scoped setting on the
+observed Neptune driver:
+
+```bash
+export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/usr/local/cuda/compat:/usr/local/nvidia/lib:/usr/local/nvidia/lib64:/usr/local/cuda/lib64
+export PYTHONPATH=/opt/olmicro-native/python
+export SGLANG_USE_SGL_FA3_KERNEL=1
+```
+
+Thirty-five focused tests passed together on the replacement L40S (twelve
+comparator/distribution, four config, six recurrence/prefill-gating, five norms,
+two partial weight-publication/repacking, three chunk solve and three activation).
+The replacement session is https://beaker.org/job/01M682TSK1EBFADEBFQB9XWGSG on
+another Neptune L40S, using the same immutable image. The first session was
+preempted after its one-hour minimum runtime; its vLLM reports were already
+committed to Weka. The final native generation/queue/reuse/reload and numerical
+matrix follows the precision fixes above; consult the experiment ledger in the
+sibling Core/vLLM checkout. Durable reports:
+`/weka/oe-adapt-default/michaeln/olmicro/native-sglang-20261030/native-fa3-final/`.
+Earlier candidate reports are kept in the parent directory. Full attention is
+qualified with `fa3`; the probe also exposes `triton` and `flashinfer` for
+diagnostics. Those alternatives were not numerically interchangeable here.
+The pinned sgl-kernel supports this backend on the L40S (SM89).
+Gated RMSNorm uses the native FLA operator that computes the FP32 SiLU gate
+product before multiplying the normalized activation.
+
+## Standalone native server
+
+With this checkout installed in the qualified environment:
+
+```bash
+unset SGLANG_EXTERNAL_MODEL_PACKAGE MILES_HYBRID_REFERENCE_BACKBONE
+export SGLANG_USE_SGL_FA3_KERNEL=1
+python -m sglang.launch_server --model-path "$CHECKPOINT" \
+  --dtype bfloat16 --tp-size 1 --context-length 4096 \
+  --attention-backend fa3 --linear-attn-backend triton \
+  --linear-attn-prefill-backend triton --linear-attn-decode-backend triton \
+  --disable-cuda-graph --disable-radix-cache --chunked-prefill-size -1 \
+  --max-running-requests 16 --mem-fraction-static 0.6
+```
+
+Existing MILES recipes explicitly select the older external bridge. They must
+be changed deliberately before a future native training run; these tests do
+not change the running Rhea experiment. Native cross-process learner weight
+publication and a full RL update remain separate training qualification gates.
